@startuml
title ExitPass Channel / Terminal Fiscal Routing

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 200
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

rectangle "Payment channels / terminals" #F7FAFF {
    component "WebPay" as WebPay
    component "APM" as APM
    component "Cashier POS" as Cashier
    component "EC Device /\nContinuity Terminal" as EC
    component "Operator-assisted\npayment" as Operator
    component "Future channels" as Future
}

component "Central PMS\nsite resolution + payment authority" as PMS
component "Resolved Site" as Site
component "Site POS Server\nfiscal authority" as POS
database "Sales Invoice issuance" as SI

WebPay --> PMS : payment context
APM --> PMS : payment context
Cashier --> PMS : payment context
EC --> PMS : continuity payment context
Operator --> PMS : assisted payment context
Future --> PMS : registered channel context

PMS --> Site : resolve Site
Site --> POS : select Site POS Server
PMS --> POS : request Sales Invoice
POS --> SI : issue for resolved Site
POS --> PMS : fiscal identity / status

note bottom of PMS
The channel does not decide fiscal authority.
Central PMS resolves the Site used for fiscal routing.
end note

note bottom of POS
The resolved Site decides which Site POS Server
issues the Sales Invoice.
end note

@enduml
